      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-algebra-2007-p2.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(-\\mathbf{3}\\). We have \\(28=x^{3}-y^{3}=(x-y)\\left(x^{2}+x y+y^{2}\\right)=(x-y)\\left((x-y)^{2}+3 x y\\right)=4 \\cdot(16+3 x y)\\), from which \\(x y=-3\\).",
